    <string name="pick_title">Add backup files</string>
    <string name="pick_desc_chats">Pick backup files by hand, e.g. SinusChat (.sinuschat). On the new phone they land in Documents/SinusChat or Documents/ETG_Chats.</string>
    <string name="pick_desc_vault">Pick vault exports by hand, e.g. 2FAS Pass / 2FAS (encrypted or plain), KeePass, Bitwarden. Restored to Documents/ETG_Vault.</string>
    <string name="pick_button">Choose files</string>
    <string name="about_author">Created by Błażej Stosio</string>
    <string name="about_github">GitHub – github.com/blazejstosio</string>
    <string name="about_technical">Data is stored in open formats (vCard 3.0, iCalendar RFC 5545, JSON, SMS Backup &amp; Restore–compatible XML). Archives are encrypted with AES-256-GCM using a key derived via PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 (210,000 iterations), and every file carries a SHA-256 checksum verified on restore. Phone-to-phone transfer uses ECDH P-256 key agreement with a fresh key per session (forward secrecy) and requires approval on the sending phone.</string>
    <string name="guide_ready_title">You are ready to install GrapheneOS</string>
    <string name="guide_ready_desc">All pre-install steps are done and your data backup is stored off the phone. Install the OS with the official installer from a computer, then come back for steps 6 and 7.</string>
    <string name="guide_ready_open_installer">Open the GrapheneOS installer</string>
    <string name="guide_done_title">Migration complete</string>
    <string name="guide_done_desc">GrapheneOS is installed and your data is restored. Once you have checked everything works, you can safely delete the backups from your USB drive or computer.</string>
